\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The turf taken
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 half a million Cloudborne and Airborne on the Domain's sacred lawn, the class lines blurring. Keep the good draft bits: homemade jumpsuits over designer clothes, Ghetto food stalls beside Airborne canap\'e9s, Channel 48 broadcasting. (canon: the draft)\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Kathy, close to Sarah
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 backstage as Sarah's doctor and her one real confidante. Not fussing over her health \'97 she knows better than anyone that Sarah doesn't break \'97 but the only person here who sees the woman under the Holy Momma: the ache, the Vegas echo, the weight of everything since. Her dry, irreverent line keeps Sarah human while she's being worshipped. When the baby stirs, Kathy feels it with her. [grounded: Kathy = Sarah's doctor and confidante, dry, warm, one of the two who know she's invincible (canon); the role is [mine]]
\f2\b Kathy and Hayley are a new couple
\f3\b0  \'97 together since "After the Barbecue" \'97 both here, a look between them across the chaos. (canon: After the Barbecue)\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Hayley, seeing it plain
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 the outsider cop, neither Airborne nor Elvi nor devotee. She's chased this whole thing the length of the story, and here it is out in the open: half a million strong, live on every screen, on the meritocracy's own lawn. Her read: the very size of the win is the danger \'97 broadcast like this, it forces the government's hand. She sees the trap inside the triumph. Not in charge of anything \'97 just seeing, with Kathy beside her. [mine \'97 my read of her; NOT security; redirect me if it's off]\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Chanta, in the green room
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 he never goes on. Sits it out backstage as band after band cycles through. Sarah passes through on her way to the stage; he sees her and keeps his distance \'97 holds the line himself. He still doesn't know what he is. (your steer; secret)\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
the High Elvis's last set
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 headlines with his band, brings Sarah out as the Holy Momma, works the crowd, builds to finish on "Religious Minds." He calls Chanta up to take a bow for the song; Chanta doesn't appear, and the show just moves on without much concern. Keep him calm and counselling, never bombast. The real songs run \'97 "Most Have Never Stirred" (the Dawkins tribute) and the rest. (your steer; log \'a7N)\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Sarah, on stage
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 invincible, so no bodily peril; the danger's all feeling. It's Vegas again and bigger, aching with everything that's passed \'97 the marriage, the isolation, the loss. She holds her detached, minimal front while it moves under her, a flicker she doesn't let show. The baby, Little Clinton, stirs. (your steer; canon: the Vegas state of grace; her detached, two-century affect)\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Dunhilton & Gerry, on the coverage
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 watching it go out live; the comic alarm (Dunhilton choking on his artisanal water); Gerry: the virus needs bringing forward. (log \'a7N; canon: the draft) Funny, not a war-room.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The close
\f3\b0 \'a0\'97 the set ends on "Religious Minds," the crowd one voice; the High Elvis's spotlit chant against religion that no one catches; in the Ghetto, Humble feels the tremor and his own flock hums "religious minds." (canon: the draft \'97 keep this)\
